#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""koine_append_db moved to `bug_db/koine_append_db` on 2026-09-17.

**This file is a tombstone and is meant to be deleted.** It holds the old name
so that the move fails loudly in the two places it would otherwise fail
silently, and it comes out once both consumers below have moved their pins.

## Why a moved file needs a marker at all

Two repositories depend on this path, and neither by accident.
[anoieu](https://github.com/ajreynol/anoieu) finds koine by probing three
directories -- `$KOINE`, `../koine`, then a clone of its own -- and asks of each
whether `koine_append_db` is a file at its root. That probe is not a path
lookup; it is anoieu's test for *is this directory koine at all*, and its own
comment says as much: "A directory without this is not koine, whatever it is
called." [dokimasia](https://github.com/ajreynol/dokimasia) keeps its own copy
of the same shim, joins the same path, and pins the same commit.

So moving the file does not break either of them. It makes a checkout of koine
stop being koine. What follows is worse than a break:

- **With cloning on**, which is the default and what CI does, `../koine` fails
  the probe and a clone at the pinned commit wins instead. That clone has the
  old layout, so everything works, and a machine that develops both repositories
  quietly stops testing the checkout it is editing.
- **With cloning off**, the probe fails everywhere and the error says koine is
  not on this machine and asks for a checkout at the path where one already is.

Neither says that a file moved, which is the only fact that would fix it.

## What this does instead

It keeps the probe passing, so `../koine` is still selected, and then says what
happened the moment anything uses it. A wrong answer delivered loudly costs an
afternoon; a right-looking answer from the wrong tree costs however long it
takes somebody to notice.

**To fix, in each:** `scripts/koine.py` names this path -- `MODULES` and
`append_db()` in anoieu, the `path / "koine_append_db"` probe in dokimasia.
Point them at `bug_db/koine_append_db`, or accept either, and move
`scripts/koine.lock` to a koine commit at or after the move.
"""

import os
import sys

MOVED = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)),
                     "bug_db", "koine_append_db")

MESSAGE = (
    "koine_append_db moved to bug_db/koine_append_db on 2026-09-17, when\n"
    "koine gave each of its two purposes a directory of its own.\n"
    f"    it is now: {MOVED}\n"
    "This file is a tombstone: it exists so this says so instead of a stale\n"
    "clone answering in its place. See its docstring for the two-line fix."
)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    print(MESSAGE, file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(2)

raise ImportError(MESSAGE)
